src/main/java/com/nordstrom/emulator/expansion/DiskLogicSequencerRom.java

These files embed PROM data transcribed from reference byte arrays in
Joao Ricardo Pagotto's Apple-Disk-II-PROM-Verify project (MIT licensed):

    https://github.com/joaopagotto/Apple-Disk-II-PROM-Verify

The transcribed data was independently cross-checked against MAME's
published checksums for the same PROMs before being trusted; see the
class-level Javadoc in each file for details.

src/main/java/com/nordstrom/emulator/expansion/DskDiskImage.java
src/main/java/com/nordstrom/emulator/expansion/DiskLogicSequencerRom.java
src/main/java/com/nordstrom/emulator/expansion/Disk2LogicSequencer.java

dfgordon/a2kit (MIT licensed) was used in three ways across these files:

    https://github.com/dfgordon/a2kit

  1. DskDiskImage's 64-entry 6-and-2 GCR translate table (TRANSLATE_62)
     is ported directly from a2kit's own FWD_62 table -- itself, per
     a2kit's own documentation, a port of the original (C++) CiderPress,
     which is BSD licensed. CiderPress's own source was never directly
     consulted or examined by this project; a2kit's MIT-licensed port of
     it is the only source actually used here, and is what this project
     is attributing.
  2. DiskLogicSequencerRom's address-bit wiring -- previously documented
     incorrectly in this project, per that file's own Javadoc -- was
     corrected by an exhaustive search for the one mapping, among
     roughly 10.3 million candidates, that reproduces a2kit's own,
     independently-sourced LSS state machine (woz_state_machine.rs)
     exactly. No code from that file is included; its documented ROM
     table was used only as a correctness target.
  3. Disk2LogicSequencer's write-mode behavior (which bit reaches the
     disk head, and when) was verified by cross-checking this project's
     own ROM table against a2kit's complete, independently-sourced table
     for every one of its 256 entries (a programmatic, exhaustive
     comparison, not a sampling) before trusting any conclusion drawn
     from it, then confirming the resulting mechanism by simulation
     against a known byte pattern. No code from a2kit is included here;
     its table was used as a verification reference, the same as in (2).

See each file's own class-level Javadoc for the specific details of how
it was used.
